Package: normet
Type: Package
Title: Meteorological Normalisation, Decomposition, and Counterfactual Modelling for Air Quality Time Series
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Congbo", "Song", email = "congbo.song@manchester.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                   comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7948-4834"))
Maintainer: Congbo Song <congbo.song@manchester.ac.uk>
Description: Provides a suite of tools for advanced air quality time series analysis.
    Core functionalities include meteorological normalisation, which normalises
    away the weather-driven variation to reveal underlying trends in data like
    air pollution concentrations, and causal inference using both classic and
    machine learning-based Synthetic Control Methods. The package features
    high-level workflows for uncertainty quantification, time-series
    decomposition, and robust placebo tests, powered by automated machine
    learning in H2O or by gradient-boosting back ends.
